              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#formalization"} Formalization
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#the_measurement_problem_2"} The Measurement Problem
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            Quantum measurement is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurement"} measurement
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
          %p
            The “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection+postulate"}> projection postulate
            ” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            asserts (
            %a{:href => "#vonNeumann32"}> von Neumann 1932
            ;
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lüders51"} Lüders 1951
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                measurement of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
                is
                %em with respect
                to a choice of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthonormal+linear+basis"} orthonormal linear basis
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %msub
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big\{\vert \psi_b \rangle \big\}_{b : B}
                of the given
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+quantum+states"} pure quantum states
            %li
              %p
                the result of measurement on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+quantum+states"} pure quantum states
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert \psi \rangle \;\in\; \mathscr{H}
                is
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    a random value
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi b
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi B
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
                %li
                  %p
                    the “
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collapse+of+the+wavefunction"}> collapse
                    ” of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
                    being measured by
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+linear+basis"} orthogonal
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection+operator"} projection
                    to the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} linear span
                    of the
                    = succeed "th" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi b
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi P
                                    %mi b
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                                %mtd
                                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                                %mtd
                                  %mover
                                    %mo →
                                    %mphantom
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                        %mo −
                                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                                    %mi b
                                  %mo ↪
                                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %mi ψ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                                %mtd
                                  %mo ↦
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi P
                                    %mi b
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %mi ψ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo =
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ψ
                                        %mi b
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ψ
                                        %mi b
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mi ψ
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          \\array{
                          P_b
                          \&amp;\colon&amp;
                          \\mathscr{H}
                          \&amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{---}}&amp;
                          \\mathscr{H}_b \hookrightarrow \mathscr{H}
                          \\\
                          \&amp;&amp;
                          \\vert \psi \rangle
                          \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                          P_b \vert \psi \rangle
                          \\mathrlap{
                          \=
                          \\vert \psi_b \rangle
                          \\langle \psi_b \vert \psi \rangle
                          }
                          }
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixed+quantum+states"} mixed quantum states
            represented by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrices"} density matrices
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+operation"} quantum operation
            which is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive-operator+valued+measure"} positive-operator valued measure
            (this is what
            %a{:href => "#Lüders51"} Lüders (1951)
            first wrote down).
          %p
            There are different ways to
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type
            the quantum measurement, taking into account the non-deterministic nature of its outcome:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Regarding the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi B
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigoplus_{b \colon B} \mathscr{H}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
                as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+disjunction"} logical disjunction
                (“or”) of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+logic"} quantum logic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
                into the direct sum whose
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi P
                          %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_b
              %blockquote
                %p
                  This choice of typing appears (briefly) in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#Selinger04"} Selinger 2004
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.mathstat.dal.ca/~selinger/papers/qpl.pdf#page=39"} p. 39
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+language"} quantum programming language
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quipper"} Quipper
            %li
              %p
                Regarding the measurement outcome
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
                as the observed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
                of the actual quantum collapse, one may regard the collapse projection as
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependently typed
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Getting from previous option back to this one is known in the the
                  = succeed "-community" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quipper"} Quipper
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "Quipper#ReferencesDynamicLifting"} dynamic lifting
                  (namely “of the measured bits back into the context”)
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/PossibleTypingsOfQuantumMeasurement-221025.jpg", :width => "560px"}/
          %p
            Both of these options naturally emerge and are naturally unified in the “
            %a{:href => "necessity+and+possibility#ModalQuantumLogic"}> Quantum Modal Logic
            ” inherent to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type+theory"} dependent linear type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+circuits+via+dependent+linear+types"} quantum circuits via dependent linear types
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/QuantumEpistemicHexagon-230806.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h2#various Various
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collapse+of+the+wavefunction"} collapse of the wavefunction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deferred+measurement+principle"} deferred measurement principle
          %div
            %h3#environmental_representation_of_measurement_channels Environmental representation of measurement channels
            %p
              By the general theorem about
              %a{:href => "quantum+channel#QuantumChannelsAndDecoherence"} environmental representations
              of quantum channels, every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+channel"} quantum channel
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
              may be decomposed as
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  coupling of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
                  to an environment/bath system
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi.mathscript ℬ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{B}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+quantum+channel"} unitary evolution
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite+system"} composite system
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi.mathscript ℬ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/averaging+quantum+channel"} averaging
                  the result over the environment states.
            %p
              The way this works specifically for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement+channels"} quantum measurement channels
              has precursor discussion
              %a{:href => "quantum+measurement#vonNeumann32"} von Neumann 1932 §VI.3
              and received much attention in discussion of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+decoherence"} quantum decoherence
              following
              %a{:href => "quantum+decoherence#Zurek81"} Zurek 1981
              and
              %a{:href => "quantum+decoherence#JoosZeh85"} Joos &amp; Zeh 1985
              (independently and apparently unkowingly of the general discussion of
              %a{:href => "quantum+channel#QuantumChannelsAndDecoherence"} environmental representations
              in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "quantum+channel#Lindblad75"} Lindblad 1975
            %p Concretely,
            %blockquote
              %p
                (we shall restrict attention to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+Hilbert+spaces"} finite-dimensional Hilbert spaces
                not to get distracted by technicalities that are irrelevant to the point we are after)
            %p
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ini
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi.mathscript ℬ
